als":78.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.11476703222292861,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":81.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.17866273873175653,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.16436843439570226,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08601559601714648,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":68.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04687997483281156,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":63.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.07765942118482738,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.014522588613991092,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":75.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00949,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Capital One Financial Corporation operates as the financial services holding company for the Capital One, National Association, which engages in the provision of various financial products and services in the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom. It operates through three segments: Credit Card, Consumer Banking, and Commercial Banking. The company accepts checking accounts, money market deposits, negotiable order of withdrawals, savings deposits, time deposits, and sweep accounts. Its loan products include credit card and personal loans; auto and retail banking loans; and commercial and multifamily real estate, and commercial and industrial loans. The company offers credit and debit card products; bank lending; and provides advisory, capital markets, net interchange, treasury management, and depository services. It serves consumers, small businesses, and commercial clients through digital channels, branches, caf\u00e9s, and other distribution channels located in New York, Louisiana, Texas, Maryland, Virginia, New Jersey, and the District of Columbia. Capital One Financial Corporation was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard D. Fairbank | Founder, Chairman, CEO & President | Age 74 | Compensation: $6.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 77K people. Revenue per employee of $689K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $337K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Capital One Financial Corporati is a large-cap financial services business with a $111.2B market cap on $53.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $26.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 11.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 25% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $42.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Real Time Payments Change The Bull Case For Capital One Financial (COF)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-cof/capital-one-financial/news/does-real-time-payments-change-the-bull-case-for-capital-one","date":"2026-11-28","timestamp":1795824923.311,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Capital One Financial (NYSE:COF) Build On Its Latest Update?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/can-capital-one-financial-nysecof-build-on-its-latest-update","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795801620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Capital One Financial (COF), What Is Behind The Latest Attention?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/capital-one-financial-cof-behind-051455793.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795670095.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Cards & Acquisition Synergies Sustain COF's Revenue Growth?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034625/will-cards-acquisition-synergies-sustain